WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.843
The fraud team flags account A-3101.

2
00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:11.779
Neo4j finds all its links in five small reads, and searches nothing.

3
00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:12.128
How?

4
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:19.401
In tables, every link lookup walks down a B+tree: three or four page reads, and more as the table grows.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:26.881
Neo4j gives every node record the same 15 bytes, so node n starts at byte n times 15.

6
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:32.974
A-3101 is node 2, so its record is at byte 30, found without a search.

7
00:00:32.974 --> 00:00:35.421
Its first relationship is 28.

8
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:42.519
Relationship records are 34 bytes, so relationship 28 is at byte 952.

9
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:45.376
It's A-3104's transfer to A-3101.

10
00:00:45.376 --> 00:00:51.301
It holds both nodes, and for each one, the previous and next relationship.

11
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:58.163
A-3101 is the second node, so the walk takes the second pair: next is 26.

12
00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:02.606
Relationship 26, a transfer to A-3103.

13
00:01:02.606 --> 00:01:06.532
Previous leads back to 28, and next is 5.

14
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.270
Relationship 5: A-3101 uses phone P-0177.

15
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:17.957
Its other pair is in P-0177's chain: one record, two chains.

16
00:01:17.957 --> 00:01:19.072
Next is 4.

17
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:21.548
Relationship 4: device D-77.

18
00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.781
Next is minus one, the end.

19
00:01:23.781 --> 00:01:27.915
Five reads found four relationships, newest first.

20
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:38.709
Crossing to a neighbour is the same move: P-0177 is node 24, at byte 360, and its chain starts at relationship 7.

21
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:47.483
The reads grow with A-3101's relationships, never with the graph: 37 relationships or 37 billion.

22
00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:52.054
Neo4j searches an index once, to find where the walk starts.

23
00:01:52.054 --> 00:01:55.637
After that, a hop is a multiplication and a read.
